@startuml
title Shelter Detail, Reviews & Submission Flow (M5)

actor Person

participant "ShelterDetailPage" as DP
participant "SubmitShelterPage" as SP
participant "ContributionsPanel" as CP
participant "ReviewForm" as RF
participant "ShelterGateway" as SHG
participant "GeoGateway" as GG
participant "GeocodeGateway" as GCG
participant "OSM Nominatim (external, client-side)" as NOM
participant "ReviewGateway" as RG
participant "AccountGateway" as AG
participant "ApiClient" as AC
participant "AuthStore" as AS
database "Spring Boot API" as API

== Shelter detail (public) ==
Person -> DP : open /shelters/123
DP -> SHG : get(123)
SHG -> AC : get<ShelterDto>('/api/shelters/123')
AC -> API : GET /api/shelters/123
API --> AC : ShelterDto (averageRating null when no reviews yet)
DP -> RG : list(123)
RG -> AC : get<ShelterReviewDto[]>('/api/shelters/123/reviews')
AC -> API : GET /api/shelters/123/reviews
API --> AC : ShelterReviewDto[]
DP --> Person : shelter info + rating summary + review list
note over DP
  Location section: a static Leaflet map (page-scoped LeafletService,
  same service as /map) zoomed to the shelter (SHELTER_ZOOM 16) with one
  non-interactive marker. No picking, no marker navigation.
end note

== My review: add / update (upsert semantics) ==
note over DP, RF
  Reviews require an authenticated, VERIFIED account (any claim).
  The detail page owns the branch (forms stay dumb): ReviewForm
  emits {rating, comment}, ShelterDetailPage makes the call.
  One review per user per shelter - the backend upserts:
  the first save of a session is always POST and returns 201
  (created) or 200 (updated a prior-session review - the page
  adopts it and switches to edit mode, PUT /mine afterwards).
end note
alt anonymous
  DP -> AS : authenticated()? no
  DP --> Person : "log in to review" -> /login?returnUrl=...
else logged in, NOT verified
  DP -> AS : isVerified()? no
  DP --> Person : banner "verify your email/phone first" -> /verify
else verified
  Person -> RF : rate 1..5 stars + optional comment (<= 500 chars)
  RF --> DP : save {rating, comment}
  DP -> RG : add(123, rating, comment)   ' first save of the session
  RG -> AC : post<ShelterReviewDto>('/api/shelters/123/reviews', body)
  AC -> API : POST /api/shelters/123/reviews
  alt 201 created / 200 updated
    API --> AC : ShelterReviewDto
    DP -> SHG : get(123)  ' and RG.list(123)
    DP --> Person : updated rating summary + review list
  else 403 (claim expired mid-session)
    API --> AC : ErrorResponse 403
    DP --> Person : banner + verify prompt
  end
end

== Edit / delete my review (session-tracked "mine") ==
note over DP, RF
  The v1 review DTO has no author identity, so the page tracks the
  user's own review in a per-session signal (06-CONTEXT decision 2).
  Fresh page load = add mode; after a save, edit mode.
end note
Person -> RF : edit stars/comment (edit mode)
RF --> DP : save {rating, comment}
DP -> RG : updateMine(123, rating, comment)
RG -> AC : put<ShelterReviewDto>('/api/shelters/123/reviews/mine', body)
AC -> API : PUT /api/shelters/123/reviews/mine
API --> AC : ShelterReviewDto
DP --> Person : review updated, summary refetched

Person -> RF : "delete my review" (edit mode only)
RF --> DP : deleteReview
DP -> RG : deleteMine(123)
RG -> AC : delete('/api/shelters/123/reviews/mine')
AC -> API : DELETE /api/shelters/123/reviews/mine
API --> AC : 204 No Content
DP --> Person : review removed, summary refetched

== Submit a shelter (verified users) ==
note over SP
  Route /submit guarded by AuthGuard + VerifiedGuard. The location
  section keeps ONE shared location signal written by FIVE capture
  modes: (1) smart text input - coordinate strings (incl. DMS, auto
  lng/lat swap), long-form map URLs parsed client-side by the pure
  parseLocationInput (shared/location-input.ts); (2) "Use my location"
  geolocation; (3) mini-map click/drag; (4) maps.app.goo.gl short links
  resolved by the backend (POST /api/geo/resolve); (5) Estonia address
  search - client-side Nominatim geocoding via GeocodeGateway (one
  deliberate request per press, hard 1 req/s spacing, always-rendered
  "(c) OpenStreetMap contributors" attribution). The read-only
  coordinate readout (+ source/swapped/accuracy hints) is a DISPLAY of
  the shared signal, not a capture mode. A FAILED capture clears the pin
  (never a silent stale pin) - a failed address SEARCH never touches the
  pin (inline state only, never blocks submit). The page pre-checks the
  Estonia bbox client-side (inline error, nothing is sent) and the
  backend re-checks (400 otherwise). capacity 1..100_000,
  description <= 2000 chars.
end note
Person -> SP : fill name, description, capacity
group capture the location (any order, repeats allowed)
  alt typed coordinates / DMS / long-form map URL
    Person -> SP : type text + Enter (or "Set location")
    SP --> Person : shared location set - marker + read-only readout
    note right of SP
      parseLocationInput: bbox gate, (lng,lat) auto-swap,
      inline error on no-pair / out-of-bounds / invalid
    end note
  else "Use my location"
    Person -> SP : click geolocation
    SP --> Person : marker at device position + accuracy hint
  else mini-map pick
    Person -> SP : click / drag the pin
    SP --> Person : shared location set (marker follows)
  else maps.app.goo.gl short link
    Person -> SP : paste short link + "Set location"
    SP -> GG : resolve(url)   ' "Resolving..." pending state
    GG -> AC : post<LocationResolved>('/api/geo/resolve', {url})
    AC -> API : POST /api/geo/resolve
    alt 200
      API --> AC : LocationResolved {latitude, longitude}
      SP --> Person : shared location set (same as a pick)
    else 400 / 429 / 502
      API --> AC : ErrorResponse
      SP --> Person : inline error (pin cleared; 429 = "try again in a minute")
    end
  else Estonia address search (client-side Nominatim)
    Person -> SP : type address + "Search" (or Enter)   ' no autosuggest
    SP -> GCG : search(query)   ' "Searching..." pending; hard 1 req/s spacing
    GCG -> NOM : GET /search?format=jsonv2&limit=5&countrycodes=ee
    NOM --> GCG : <= 5 results (display name + string lat/lon)
    GCG --> SP : results (429 -> "please wait a moment"; network -> generic copy)
    Person -> SP : pick a result
    SP --> Person : shared location set + address field prefilled ONLY IF empty
    note right of SP
      A failed SEARCH (no results / 429 / network) never touches the pin -
      inline state only, never blocks submit.
    end note
  end
end
SP -> SHG : create(request)
SHG -> AC : post<ShelterDto>('/api/shelters', body)
AC -> API : POST /api/shelters
alt 201 Created + Location header
  API --> AC : ShelterDto (source=USER, status=ACTIVE)
  SP --> Person : navigate('/shelters/{id}')
else 401 anonymous / 403 not verified / 400 out-of-Estonia
  API --> AC : ErrorResponse
  SP --> Person : banner with message (input preserved; 403 adds a /verify link)
end

note over DP
  USER-submitted rows are sacred on the backend: the registry
  importer never touches source=USER shelters. Author-scoped
  management (M8) is the one exception - see below.
end note

== Manage my contributions (M8, account page) ==
note over CP
  The /account page's "My contributions" panel (ContributionsPanel,
  embedded in AccountPage). Both lists load in parallel; each has its
  own loading/empty/error states. Edits are inline-expanding forms
  (no modals); deletes are two-step confirms (no window.confirm).
end note
Person -> CP : open /account
== shelters list ==
CP -> SHG : mine()
SHG -> AC : get<ShelterDto[]>('/api/shelters/mine')
AC -> API : GET /api/shelters/mine (Bearer JWT)
API --> CP : ShelterDto[] (the caller's USER rows only)
== reviews list ==
CP -> AG : myReviews()
AG -> AC : get<MyReviewDto[]>('/account/reviews/mine')
AC -> API : GET /account/reviews/mine (Bearer JWT)
API --> CP : MyReviewDto[] (shelterId + shelterName + rating + comment)
Person -> CP : edit a shelter row (inline form)
CP -> SHG : update(id, name/lat/lng/description/capacity)
SHG -> AC : put<ShelterDto>('/api/shelters/{id}', body)
alt 200 updated
  API --> CP : ShelterDto -> row updated in place (no page reload)
else 400 (bbox/fields) / 403 (not the author) / 404 (absent)
  API --> CP : ErrorResponse -> banner via bannerMessage, row unchanged
end
Person -> CP : delete a shelter (two-step confirm: reviews go too)
CP -> SHG : remove(id)
SHG -> AC : delete('/api/shelters/{id}')
AC -> API : DELETE /api/shelters/{id}
API --> CP : 204 No Content -> row removed (reviews cascade)
Person -> CP : edit a review row (rating 1..5 + comment)
CP -> RG : updateMine(shelterId, rating, comment)
RG -> AC : put<ShelterReviewDto>('/api/shelters/{id}/reviews/mine', body)
AC -> API : PUT /api/shelters/{id}/reviews/mine
API --> CP : ShelterReviewDto -> row updated in place
Person -> CP : delete a review (two-step confirm)
CP -> RG : deleteMine(shelterId)
RG -> AC : delete('/api/shelters/{id}/reviews/mine')
AC -> API : DELETE /api/shelters/{id}/reviews/mine
API --> CP : 204 No Content -> row removed
@enduml
